Third-party software
====================

None of the software below is vendored in this repository. Each keeps its own license.

CLIProxyAPI
  https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI
  License: MIT
  codexpool downloads CLIProxyAPI's upstream release source from GitHub at install and upgrade time and builds
  it with one added file, build/codexpool_gate.go (the origin gate), and a one-line change to
  cmd/server/main.go that registers the gate. CLIProxyAPI is not vendored here, and its MIT license applies
  to it.

PyObjC (pyobjc-core, pyobjc-framework-Cocoa)
  https://github.com/ronaldoussoren/pyobjc
  License: MIT
  Installed from PyPI into codexpool's own Python environment at install time, for the menu bar app, the
  Settings window and the Setup assistant.

Go
  https://go.dev
  License: BSD 3-Clause
  The official Go toolchain is downloaded from go.dev at install time, checked against its published SHA-256,
  and used only to build CLIProxyAPI.

uv
  https://github.com/astral-sh/uv
  License: Apache-2.0 or MIT
  install.sh installs uv from Astral only on a Mac with no Python 3.11 or newer, and only after asking (or
  with --yes); uv then provides that Python.

CodexBar
  The menu bar design borrows CodexBar's visual language. No CodexBar code is used.
